      "qualification": "No assertion that it does or does not subsume the candidate. No unrecorded construction is presented as literature."
    },
    "3": {
      "verdict": "SUBSUMED",
      "subject": "Published explicit examples",
      "source": {
        "authors": [
          "Hyun Jin Kim",
          "Whan-Hyuk Choi",
          "Yoonjin Lee"
        ],
        "title": "Construction of reversible self-dual codes",
        "journal": "Finite Fields and Their Applications 67 (2020), 101714",
        "doi": "10.1016/j.ffa.2020.101714",
        "available_online": "2020-07-14",
        "theorem": "5.1, printed p.15",
        "definitions": "Section 2, printed p.3",
        "explicit_matrices": "printed p.16",
        "url": "https://yis.yonsei.ac.kr/liberaledu/activities/research.do?articleNo=143562&attachNo=123378&mode=download",
        "sha256": "12aaacaea7436b3dad3a7a3a47c5477a8a150405e685a420cc6cf1247a1f0f27"
      },
      "normalized_theorem": "There exist at least nine pairwise inequivalent reversible binary self-dual [70,35,12] codes whose full coordinate-permutation automorphism groups each have order 2.",
      "bridge": "For each such code, reversal tau=(1 70)(2 69)...(35 36) is in PAut by Section 2. It is nonidentity and has no fixed coordinate. Since the FULL group has order 2, PAut={1,tau}. Hence the code is a quasi group code for its free subgroup PAut, at length 70=2*35>2. This contradicts the universal arXiv Conjecture 4.9.",
      "explicitness": "The property is explicitly published; identifying it as a counterexample to the later conjecture is the present elementary bridge. Not merely an abstract-group realization.",
      "validation": "Four 35x35 A matrices extracted from printed p.16. Independently checked AA^T=I and A=R A^T R, so [I|A] is self-dual and reversal invariant. Full automorphism order and distance are read published results, not independently recomputed in this lane.",
      "evidence": [
        "receipts/reversible2020.pdf",
        "bodies/reversible2020.txt",
        "matrix-validation.json",
        "validate_matrices.py",
        "bodies/published-A1.txt",
        "bodies/published-A2.txt",
        "bodies/published-A3.txt",
        "bodies/published-A4.txt"
      ],
      "asymptotic_subquestion": {
        "verdict": "UNRESOLVED",
        "finding": "No read theorem that almost all binary codes conditioned to admit a fixed-point-free involution have exactly that full group. Unconditioned rigidity is insufficient. No such theorem is needed after the explicit 2020 result."
      }
    },
    "4": {
      "verdict": "UNRESOLVED",
      "subject": "Later 2023-2026 status and journal conjecture reconciliation",
      "finding": "No read later body resolving or restating Conjecture 4.9 in full was found. Current arXiv 2402.10667 PDF is v3, 6 January 2026: On the permutation automorphisms of binary cubic codes, by Murat Altunbulak, Fatma Altunbulak Aksu, Roghayeh Hafezieh and Ipek Tuvay. Introduction p.1 restates only the original dimension/codimension <=4 C2 nonexistence result; its main results and concluding Conjecture 5.5 concern C3. This updates the prior reviewer v1-only screen. Journal [1] is now cited as J. Algebra Appl.24 (2025), Paper2550137. Bouyuklieva 2309.05288 examples/conclusion do not settle C2. OpenAlex citing query returns zero despite this known citation, so metadata is incomplete. Journal Conjecture 4.9 body still unreconciled.",
